# A Luxel library scene (Gitea #785) — Apache-2.0. Grammar: library/README.md.
# `fit tile`: one 7x7 sprite repeated across the layout and ADDED over a
# pattern. Two things worth knowing are in these four lines. The box is an
# explicit 64x64; since #985 a 0x0 box under `tile` means the whole layout too
# (docs/spec/scenes.md §4), while under `fill`/`contain` it would draw the
# sprite once at its natural size. And the pattern runs at 60 % so the sparks
# have somewhere to add INTO — added over a saturated frame they are invisible.
S - Spark Field
L pat 0 0 0 0 normal 60 none fill 1
N Twirls
I @pat/2d-spiral-twirls
L sprite 0 0 64 64 add 100 none tile 1
N Sparks
I @spr/spark
